# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MOASYS-Vault — Shows ignore list (EXAMPLE)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# A "do not warn me about this" list for your shows library. Anything listed
# here is silently dropped from output/<drive>/shows/warnings.json and
# validation-warnings.json on every run, and counted in the run summary.
#
# Ignore lists are per DRIVE as well as per type, because warning paths are
# relative to that drive's root_path. `ignored/server/shows.yaml` only affects
# runs against the root named "Server".
#
# How to use this file:
#   1. Copy it to `ignored/<drive>/shows.yaml` (drop the `.example` suffix).
#      The real file is gitignored so your personal decisions stay out of
#      version control.
#   2. Add names under the level they belong to.
#   3. Re-run `npm run shows <drive>`. Matching warnings disappear.
#
# ── Levels ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   folders    a category folder   - Other HD
#   shows      one show            - Firefly (2002)
#   seasons    one season          - Band of Brothers (2001)/Specials
#   episodes   one episode         - My Name Is Earl (2005)/S03E01
#
# Names are matched at their own level and are CATEGORY-INDEPENDENT: a show
# listed here is silenced whether it lives in HD/, Other SD/, or both. That is
# also what lets an entry reach warn_multi_quality and warn_duplicate_quality,
# which report `Show (YEAR) — Season N` with no category to anchor to.
#
# ── Two conveniences specific to shows ───────────────────────────────────────
#
#   - `Season 3` and `Season 03` are the same entry. The scan pass reports the
#     on-disk folder name; the TMDB pass reports the parsed season number. One
#     entry covers both.
#   - An `episodes:` entry may be written as the S03E01 code OR as the full
#     filename. Either form silences both the scan pass's warnings about that
#     file and the TMDB pass's episode-title warning about that code.
#
# ── Qualifiers ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# `seasons:` and `episodes:` entries must name their show — a bare `Season 01`
# or episode filename would match in every show in the library. A `/` means
# "somewhere above", not "immediately above", so `Show (2020)/S03E01` is fine
# even though a season sits between them.
#
# ── Scope ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# An entry silences EVERY warning at or below its level — episode gaps, TMDB
# counts, naming, quality, all of them. There is no per-warning-type scoping.
# To turn off a whole warning type instead, set `checks.warn_*: false` in
# rules/shows.yaml.
#
# ── Matching ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Exact per level (not a prefix, so `Firefly (2002)` does not match
# `Firefly Serenity (2005)`), case-insensitive, and either slash works.
#
# ── Finding names ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Take them from the `path` values in output/<drive>/shows/warnings.json and
# validation-warnings.json, dropping the leading category folder.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# Silence everything under a category folder
# folders:
#   - Other HD
#   - Other SD


# Silence a whole show you can't fix
# (Use this when a show has known missing episodes — never released, culled by
# the rights holder — and you don't want warn_episode_gaps /
# warn_tmdb_episode_count noise on every run.)
# shows:
#   - Channel 4 Catchup (2024)
#   - Firefly (2002)


# Silence one season
# (The rest of the show's warnings stay live. `Season 2` and `Season 02` are
# the same entry.)
# seasons:
#   - Some Show (2020)/Season 2
#   - Band of Brothers (2001)/Specials


# Silence one episode
# (Either form works and both cover every pass:)
# episodes:
#   - Some Show (2020)/S01E05
#   - Some Show (2020)/Season 01/Some Show (2020) - S01E05 - Title.mp4
